# Freenove 4WD Car Kit ESP32 — runtime + test suite.
# Partition: 448 KB LittleFS (partitions_4M_ota_trim.csv) = 112 blocks @ 4KB.
# 4KB-block LittleFS usage: ~46 blocks data + ~6 dir/superblock meta = ~52 blocks; ~60 free.
# Added (2026-06-27) rxrs-tests (~6 blk), r5rs-pitfall (~3), gc-pause-bench (~1),
# lamblisp-tests (~13) = ~23 blk -> ~75/112 used, ~37 free. Still fits; verify on flash.
# Omitted vs S3 devkit: llip-server, rsa, dh_groups, rxrs_ai_overrides (redundant w/ r7rs).
# Conform = r7rs+rxrs+r5rs-pitfall. Extend = ll-extensions + lamblisp-tests.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/Freenove-4WD-Car-Kit-ESP32.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/Sonar.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/I2C.scm
core/Wire.scm
core/PCA9685.scm
core/PCF8574.scm
core/WS2812.scm
core/LightSensor.scm
core/LCD1602.scm
core/array.scm

# P123 robot stack — cooperative behaviour queue, LED ring service, LLIP framing + signals
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Leds.scm
features/llip-frame.scm
features/llip-signals.scm
features/llip-executor.scm
features/llip-reactive.scm

# P123 Part D: carry a camera frame over LLIP as BINARY (s-expression header + raw bytes).
# NOT base64 -- every LambLisp port is already a binary port, so a JPEG rides the same TCP
# connection the move programs use, unencoded.  Codec only: it loads on a board with no camera.
features/llip-vision.scm

# Proximity alarm: WS2812 ring (and optionally an onboard LED) flashing faster as the target
# nears.  Non-blocking tick, so it can share the 3 ms loop with Sonar.loop and the B5 reflex.
features/sonar-flash.scm

# P126 R6 arms A2 (blocking Sonar.ping) and A3 (ISR Sonar.start/Sonar.result), in one file so the
# two cannot drift apart -- they must sample the same target in the same session to be comparable.
tests/ll_tests/sonar-bench.scm

# Serial file tunnel: resident LLIP receiver (host = w3_ai_scripts/llip_tunnel.py)
features/llip-serial.scm

# LLIP SERVER -- filesystem operations for a remote LambLisp client.  Added 2026-09-12: EVERY
# PUBLISHED TARGET SUPPORTS LLIP BY DEFAULT.  This target staged the serial RECEIVER below but not
# the SERVER, so `llip ls/send/run` against it answered nothing -- a capability the customer's own
# `tools/llip` CLI advertises, shipped half-present.  The two halves are not interchangeable:
# llip-serial.scm is the resident (llt) that accepts a serial session; llip-server.scm is what
# serves the file operations inside it.
tools/llip-server.scm

# R5RS/R7RS overrides
rxrs/rxrs.scm
rxrs/rxrs_cxr.scm
rxrs/rxrs_exceptions.scm
rxrs/rxrs_continuations.scm
rxrs/rxrs_promises.scm
rxrs/rxrs_quasiquote.scm
rxrs/rxrs_syntax.scm
rxrs/rxrs_library.scm
rxrs/rxrs_srfi.scm

# Board-specific init
boards/Freenove-4WD-Car-Kit-ESP32.scm

# Perf/gcpause bench files only (small).  The correctness tiers (smoke/conform/subsystem/extend)
# are delivered INCREMENTALLY per-tier by _w3_run_correct_esp32 (stage runtime + that tier's files
# -> uploadfs -> load), so the ~460KB ll_tests suite is NOT shipped here -- it does not fit the
# 448KB LittleFS partition all at once.  Only the perf/gcpause bench files (loaded from FS by the
# perf/gcpause runners) stay resident.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm   -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm     -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm -> ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/pause_bench.scm    -> ll_tests/pause_bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm -> ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm
#
# B65, MEASURED 2026-09-15 against the partition table this env ACTUALLY BUILDS WITH.
# All three of B65's missing files now ship.  They fit because the 4WD moved to the llloader
# layout in 7d90224 (2026-09-13): `partitions_4M_ota.csv` -- factory=llloader (1152 KB, the C
# recovery root), ota_0=the VM (2368 KB), storage=512 KB, and NO ota_1.  Dropping the OTA spare is
# what paid for all of it; that table's own header says the single-ota_0 layout "retires B65".
#
# THE FIRST PASS OF THIS NOTE WAS WRONG AND IS KEPT AS THE WARNING.  It concluded only two of the
# three could ship, from mklittlefs runs at `-s 0x070000` -- 448 KB, taken from
# `partitions_4M_ota_trim.csv` because B65's registry entry names that file.  NOTHING BUILDS WITH
# THAT TABLE.  No .ini and no board JSON references it; it is an orphan left behind by the move.
# The real slot is 0x080000.  Measuring carefully against the wrong geometry is not measuring.
#
# Verified at the REAL size (-p 256 -b 4096 -s 0x080000): image builds rc=0 with all three added.
# Re-run that before adding ANY file here, and take the size from platformio.ini's
# board_build.partitions for THIS env -- never from a registry entry or a comment, this one
# included.
file: tests/ll_tests/rxrs-tests.scm     -> ll_tests/rxrs-tests.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/lamblisp-tests.scm -> ll_tests/lamblisp-tests.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/r5rs-pitfall.scm  -> ll_tests/r5rs-pitfall.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
# Peer CA for the `network` test_id: written by _w3_run_network, absent otherwise (untracked).
optional: runtime-defaults/net-test-ca.pem -> net-test-ca.pem
# Bench WiFi credentials: untracked, absent by default, silent when absent (see .example).
#
# (HISTORICAL, superseded 2026-09-17 -- see the staged line below.)  NOT STAGED ON THIS TARGET -- B411.  The bench Settings-local.scm carries `(wifi . 1)` for every
# board, and on this part that is FATAL rather than merely expensive: WiFi.begin() reserves the
# radio's rx/tx buffers at setup.scm load time, internal DRAM is already down to ~45 KB free /
# 26 KB largest by then, and the allocation that fails is the mutex uart_write needs -- so the
# board aborts in lock_init_generic and reboots, forever, with no message explaining why.
# Measured 2026-09-14 by controlled comparison on this board: `(wifi . 1)` boot-loops,
# `(wifi . 0)` boots to a REPL.  Credentials were correct in both cases; this is not a
# bad-password problem.
#
# WiFi.scm's own comment already says the connect is "critical on the 2MB-PSRAM" board (B60's
# lesson) -- the defect is that a GLOBAL bench override silently re-enables it on the tightest
# board in the fleet.  Staging is the per-target mechanism, so the decision belongs here.
#
# THE RADIO STILL WORKS.  This only removes the AUTO-CONNECT at boot; an app calls
# (WiFi.begin ssid pass) when it actually needs it, which is exactly the contract WiFi.scm
# documents.  Re-add the line if this board ever gets a memory budget that can afford it.
# STAGED AGAIN 2026-09-17 -- B411's measurement is SUPERSEDED, not repealed by opinion.
# B411 was measured 2026-09-14 and was correct THEN: WiFi.begin() reserves the radio's buffers at
# setup.scm load time, and by then internal DRAM was down to ~45 KB free / 26 KB largest, so the
# allocation that failed was the mutex uart_write needs -- abort in lock_init_generic, reboot,
# forever, with no message saying why.
#
# WHAT CHANGED IS *WHEN* THE RADIO TAKES ITS MEMORY, WHICH IS THE WHOLE OF [P211] PHASE 0.
# ll_xmop3_WiFi.cpp:497 now asks ll_wifi_wanted_at_boot() IN THE INSTALLER -- before setup.scm
# loads a line of Scheme -- and reserves LL_WIFI_RESERVE_BYTES (48 KB) through ll_fastram while the
# heap is still contiguous.  WiFi.begin() later RELEASES that reservation immediately before it
# allocates, so the radio lands in a hole kept for it rather than competing for what is left.
# The sibling WROVER is the same SoC with the same constraint and went from -49,100 to +3,836 on
# exactly this change, which is why its own line (Freenove-ESP32-WROVER.manifest:95) is live.
#
# SO THIS IS A TEST, NOT A BELIEF.  If the board boot-loops it goes straight back to commented and
# B411 is re-opened with a second measurement; recovery is a reflash from the Jetson.
optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm -> Settings-local.scm
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm
